atem:
  line: Mara Okafor and the narrator defend the Hollins Lane orchard by challenging the council's July mowing plan
    that threatens pollinators.
  focus: The text contrasts the orchard's improved yield with the danger of early mowing, directing attention to
    the need for pollinators.
  push: The author wants the reader to support delaying the mowing until September to protect the orchard's fruit
    production.
  pull: The text assumes the meadow strip is the sole source of pollinators and ignores the lease's legal ambiguity
    regarding mowing rights.
